4c:["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"05"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"Implementation"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":"The setup is Coolify on an Ubuntu host: applications deploy from connected GitHub repositories into containers, Coolify's proxy layer terminates TLS and routes configured domains, and DNS records at the registrar point traffic at the host. Environment variables and build configuration live per-application inside Coolify, keeping deployment concerns out of application code."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"The workflow is deliberately boring: push to a branch, deploy, watch the logs, verify the domain, fix what's broken. The interesting part is the diagnostic muscle it builds — when a deployment fails, the cause can live anywhere in a chain from DNS propagation to proxy configuration to the application itself, and finding it requires reading each layer honestly."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5","children":[["$","span","Coolify",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"Coolify"}],["$","span","Docker",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"Docker"}],["$","span","Ubuntu",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"Ubuntu"}],["$","span","DNS",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"DNS"}],["$","span","GitHub",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"GitHub"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
4d:["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"06"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"Engineering challenges"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5 sm:grid-cols-[110px_minmax(0,1fr)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"label-mono text-muted-foreground","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/80","children":"DNS is the classic trap: records propagate asynchronously, caches lie, and 'it works for me' is meaningless across resolvers."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sm:border-l sm:border-border sm:pl-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"label-mono text-accent-blue","children":"Approach"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"A fixed diagnostic order — registrar, resolver caches, direct DNS queries, then the proxy — plus the discipline to wait out propagation instead of reconfiguring a correct setup out of impatience."}]]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5 sm:grid-cols-[110px_minmax(0,1fr)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"label-mono text-muted-foreground","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/80","children":"When a containerised app fails behind a proxy, the error you see is rarely the error that happened."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sm:border-l sm:border-border sm:pl-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"label-mono text-accent-blue","children":"Approach"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"Reading logs at every layer in sequence: container stdout, proxy access and error logs, then the application. The proxy's 502 is a symptom; the cause is usually one layer deeper."}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}]}]
